+
+Status while drafting: **UNSEALED**.
+
+## 1. Cross outcome: decide normalization first
+
+The four blinds substantially deduplicate into two questions. Root, Astra and
+Sol all put the missing incoming `75/125 -> standard F2` arrow ahead of another
+receiver calculation; their proposed `M2=90` audits are alternative fallbacks
+to the same source question. Fable's reduced-base programme is the distinct
+idea, but its claimed automatic reconstruction omits a term that can invalidate
+its first contact estimate. The threshold lemma in the Sol blind is a valid
+abstract refinement with little present source value. Accordingly I recommend
+two actionable cards total, ranked below, and no computation.
+
+The first provisional composition has the exact chain
+
+```text
+actual ordinary constant-J pair of actual degrees 75,125
+ -> ML polynomial source rectangle for that given pair
+ -> ordinary GGV (3,5)-pair with endpoint 3(a,b), a+b <= 25
+ -> endpoint-preserving standardization
+ -> published complete-chain table; only F2 with (a,b)=(5,20)
+ -> accepted standard-F2 receiver map and accepted15q exclusion.
+```
+
+My hand audit finds the new internal degree comparison coherent. Once the first
+coordinate has a genuine joint rectangle corner `(r,s)`, every positive-weight
+leader is that monomial. Vanishing of the leading bracket forces each
+positive-weight leader of the mate onto the same ray; the total-weight leader
+then dominates for every positive weight, so the mate has its own proportional
+rectangle. Applying the inverse source automorphism with component degrees
+`M,N >= 1` gives exact, cancellation-free degrees because the corner uniquely
+maximizes `Mi+Nj`. Thus `(r,s)=3(a,b)`, the mate corner is `5(a,b)`, and
+`25=Ma+Nb >= a+b`. The hand filter of the imported table leaves only F2.
+Then `25=5M+20N` forces `M=N=1`, so the selected normalizer is affine and the
+actual degrees are retained. This does not use global minimality, an
+arbitrary target degree reduction, or Strinz as proof authority.
+
+That is an audit of the composition's logic, not promotion. Its load-bearing
+inputs remain the exact ML given-representative rectangle theorem, GGV
+standardization, and the GGHV table's completeness/applicability. The charged
+primary audit confirms their stated interfaces at imported-primary trust, but
+the separately running different-model gate is forbidden here. Its verdict,
+not cross agreement, must determine lifecycle.
+
+If that gate confirms every arrow, accepted15q conditionally excludes every
+actual ordinary characteristic-zero pair of **exact degrees** `(75,125)`.
+It does not prove a maximum-degree-125 theorem, exclude every `D125` label, or
+extend to arbitrary degree. The `M2=90` line remains distinct from `M2=105`
+and from F2 as characteristic data, but an attained `M2=90` parent would still
+be an actual `75/125` pair and is therefore impossible by the upstream theorem;
+no child signature or receiver construction then has mathematical value.
+Likewise, the complete guarded B0 ideal is geometrically empty only if its
+already stated all-row reconstruction and exact degree guard are retained;
+this yields no displayed unit or cofactor certificate. If the gate instead
+finds a gap, stop at its first failed arrow. Only then should the literal
+`M2=90` source signature be extracted; shared `7/5`, degree labels, or the
+`M2=105` descent are not replacements for the missing map.
+
+The second provisional conclusion is separate: normalization plus the first
+assertion of GGV Corollary 7.9 would make the entire ordinary constant-J,
+coprime-ratio, closed-common-root class empty. If confirmed, accepted15w is not
+contradicted. Its late-contact implication is a correct theorem on a
+hypothetical class whose actual source antecedent is empty; the finite late-T
+lemma itself remains a nonvacuous algebraic instrument. Thus neither the new
+whole-class screen nor accepted15w supplies a new client. The supplied GGV
+Theorem 2.6 endpoint statement also rules out the proposed balanced
+`H0=xy` Keller control: its sole positive-total-weight endpoint is `(k,k)`,
+forbidden by item (4). This is an actual endpoint obstruction, not a claim
+that every unequal proper-power root is excluded.
+
+## 2. Proper-power reconstruction and the threshold proposal
+
+Fable's useful observation is only the factor-level start: if a common leader
+is `H=h^e`, replacing it by a primitive closed root changes the leading scalar
+exponents from `(3,5)` to `(3e,5e)`. It does **not** preserve the old cubic/
+quintic reference identity. Let the actual scalar references be `a(R),b(R)`
+and divide in the scalar polynomial ring
+
+```text
+b'(z) = a'(z)q(z) + rho(z).
+```
+
+For `A=a(R)+F` and `B=b(R)+q(R)F+G`, direct factored bracket bookkeeping gives
+
+```text
+[A,B] = [R,T] + [F,G],
+T = a'(R)G - rho(R)F - (q'(R)/2)F^2.
+```
+
+This identity is sound as a formal algebraic decomposition, but it is not a
+source implication and does not establish `ord_s G >= 2j`. In the `(3e,5e)`
+homogeneous ledger the first allowed derivative-remainder coefficient can
+occur at order `(2e+1)d`, where `d=deg h`. Hence `rho(R)F` can have order
+`(2e+1)d+j`, strictly before `2j` whenever `j>(2e+1)d`. The induction that
+normalizes the leading coefficient of `G` must retain this term and every
+kernel; the old `(3,5)` proof cannot be imported by renaming `H` to `h`.
+Fable Card B explicitly includes `ord G>=2j` among its starting data and so
+does not prove the claimed general late-contact bound. Its reduced-base
+universality is, at most, an unreviewed reference *frame*; its main estimate is
+`OPEN` in substance, though I introduce no new campaign OPEN identifier.
+
+The first honest unequal proper-power method control is
+
+```text
+h = x*y^10,  e=2,  H=h^2,
+tops h^6 and h^10, actual-degree scale (66,110).
+```
+
+Here `h` has two unequal coprime factor multiplicities, so the supplied
+balanced-endpoint theorem does not reject it. The degree gcd is `22>=16` and
+maximum degree `110>=108`, so the charged classical numerical screens do not
+already close this scale; `D=21` would still have maximum `105<108`, making
+`D=22` the first integer scale for this ratio beyond that screen. This remains
+a method control, not a claimed Keller pair or a claim that arbitrary scalar
+data arise from one. It is particularly discriminating without any expansion:
+`d=11,e=2` gives first possible `rho` order `55`, while the natural late
+inequality `3j>(8e-1)d=165` begins at `j=56`; throughout that late range the
+`rho F` term can precede `F^2`. A proof must either derive its vanishing from a
+literal source or replace the `2j` bound. Merely choosing coefficients that
+make `rho=0` would be a predicate flip, not an attack on the full claim.
+
+The Sol blind's separate finite-centralizer assertion
+
+```text
+deg_combined(T) <= N and ord_s[R,T] >= N  =>  [R,T]=0
+```
+
+survives my prose audit as an abstract candidate. Split `T` into combined-
+homogeneous pieces; their brackets have distinct combined degrees. In a piece
+of degree `n<=N`, every first coefficient at order `ell<n` lies in `K[H]` and
+can be removed by the matching `s^ell R^i`; if `ell=n`, the coefficient has
+ordinary degree zero and already commutes. Finite induction exhausts the
+piece. This is still unreviewed cross mathematics, not promoted. Its only
+stated application adds the equality boundary `3j=7D` (hence only the relevant
+divisibility cases) to accepted15w. If the provisional whole closed-H screen
+passes, that application has no actual source; if it fails, the packet still
+names no attached client. Bank it as a method-control candidate and do not
+spend a gate before a literal source makes equality decisive.
+
+Finally, Fable's proposed tame monomial-J countermodel is an honest
+changed-object control only if its computed characteristic packet satisfies
+every hypothesis of the cited shifted Moh statement. Without the exact
+charged proposition and a matching nontrivial packet, failure would test a
+different predicate. It therefore does not outrank the existing normalization
+gate or license a trust-perimeter reversal.
+
