+## 4. Portfolio, history, and systems disposition
+
+**Proof direction.** Continue Card 1 to its already scheduled verdict. Beyond
+fixed degree, the strongest direction is still a genuine source-and-coverage
+theorem: a hybrid route owes `G2-PSC` before using GGV data in a Sigray tree;
+a pure Sigray route may bypass that arrow but still owes its own source,
+all-branch landing, off-axis coverage, and a cofinal type/degree bound.
+`G2-BD` is the later bounded-delay obligation and is not a synonym. The
+proper-power scalar ledger in Card 2 is the sharpest local next probe only
+after such a source is literal. An abstract theorem with no unretired family
+is a method control, not a new client.
+
+**Stop/redesign.** Stop all work on the six standard-F2 receivers and the
+named `M2=105` receiver except correction of a proved interface. Do not launch
+the Sol equality lemma merely because its proof appears short. Redesign the
+reference method around `(3e,5e)`, `rho`, and all kernels, not around a
+notation-preserving substitution. Keep K16's all-`m` product locus and `b=0`
+boundary visible but idle. Characteristic-`p`/Witt work remains at its
+unbounded polynomiality and exterior-conductor boundary; fixed support caps
+do not answer it. Proper Galois second-leg quotients and
+`d2=[K:C(f,g)]=2` remain closed by BD-GAL. The distinct `d1=2`, non-Galois
+`d2>=3`, and primitive cases remain open; none is renamed or relaunched here.
+
+**Historical corrections.** The original frozen manifest contains **31
+entries**, and the manifest itself makes **32 files**. The blind-Sol premise
+"30 entries plus manifest/appendix" is false; a directory-count discrepancy
+did not show missing scientific bytes. Historical avenue scores are not
+current ranks, so this cross changes no full 46-vector. The Fable collection
+lapse is also stated narrowly: root's first whole-body read preceded completion
+of current-pin checks because a comparison expected `CLEAN_SEALED` while the
+valid receipt status was `CLEAN`. Subsequent pins passed and no live body was
+read. This is an ordering defect, not lost content and not a receipt-first
+success.
+
+**One earned systems change.** Make the existing root collector's terminal-
+status comparison accept the documented `CLEAN` value while checking
+`BODY_SEALED` and `ABSENT` in their separate fields, and make any hash/status
+failure stop before body open. One fixture for a valid
+`DONE=0/CLEAN/BODY_SEALED/ABSENT` receipt and one bad-hash negative fixture are
+enough. The benefit is concrete: it removes the exact condition that induced
+this round's ordering lapse without adding a new artifact layer. Root owns any
+implementation; none is made here. Do not add the proposed launch overlay,
+checker farm, duplicate lemma sheet, scheduler, or packet machinery. The
+overlay argument partly relied on the false count, the current PINS/poststate
+already exposed the discrepancy, and the reported byte reduction measures
+context size rather than mathematical throughput.
